================================================================================
BEFORE / AFTER — deploy-web-admin.sh scp/atomic-swap race fix
================================================================================

REMOTE TARBALL PATH HANDLING
----------------------------

BEFORE (scripts/deploy/deploy-web-admin.sh @ origin/main 51a9e6440)

  L197:  scp -q "$TMP_TAR" "$GATEWAY:/tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz"
  L198:  log "   ✓ 上传完成"
  L214:  tar xzf /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz -C "\$STAGING"
  L238:  rm -f /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz
  L277:  scp -q "$TMP_TAR" "$GATEWAY:/tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz"   (prod)
  L292:  tar xzf /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz -C "\$STAGING"          (prod)
  L312:  rm -f /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz                           (prod)

  Issue: SHARED HARDCODED REMOTE PATH across all concurrent deploys.
  Race: deploy A's tar xzf can be defeated by deploy B's rm -f in the
  ~1-3s gap between scp and tar. Symptom: "✓ 上传完成" then
  tar: Cannot open /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz.


AFTER (this branch)

  L196: # May 13 2026 race fix: per-PID remote tarball path eliminates
  L197: # concurrent-deploy collision on shared /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz.
  L198: # ... [comment block explaining root cause] ...
  L202: REMOTE_TAR="/tmp/web-admin-dist.$$.tar.gz"
  L203: log "📤 [3/4] 上传到 $GATEWAY (remote: $REMOTE_TAR)..."
  L204: scp -q "$TMP_TAR" "$GATEWAY:$REMOTE_TAR"
  L205:
  L206: # Post-scp verify: defense in depth ...
  L210: LOCAL_SIZE=$(stat -c %s "$TMP_TAR" ...)
  L211: REMOTE_SIZE=$(ssh "$GATEWAY" "stat -c %s '$REMOTE_TAR' ...")
  L212: if [ "$REMOTE_SIZE" != "$LOCAL_SIZE" ]; then
  L213:     log "❌ post-scp verify FAILED: ..."
  L214:     ...
  L216:     exit 1
  L217: fi
  L218: log "   ✓ 上传完成 (verified ${LOCAL_SIZE}B match)"

  All 6 hardcoded references replaced with $REMOTE_TAR (per-PID).
  Both heredocs (test + prod) use $REMOTE_TAR.
  Both scp blocks (test + prod) followed by verify.


